NAME
    wmpaint - tiny paint program WM client (Path C phase 9)

SYNOPSIS
    wmpaint [SECONDS]

DESCRIPTION
    Open a 400x280 WM window with a top toolbar of 7 color
    swatches and a canvas below.  Drag the left mouse button to
    paint smooth strokes (Bresenham line between every two
    MOUSE_MOVE events with a configurable brush radius).

    Mouse:
      L click in toolbar    select color 1..7
      L drag in canvas      paint stroke at current color/radius
      L release             lift the pen

    Keyboard (focus the window first):
      1..7    select color (white/red/yellow/green/cyan/blue/magenta)
      + / -   bigger / smaller brush
      c       clear canvas
      Ctrl-S  save canvas to /tmp/paint.ppm (P6 PPM, 400x256)
      q       quit

    Exit after SECONDS (default 60) or 'q' or window close.

    Save (session 150): pressing Ctrl-S writes the canvas area
    (everything below the 24-px toolbar) to /tmp/paint.ppm as
    a binary P6 PPM.  A toast notification confirms the save
    with the byte count.  Re-open the result via:

        wmview /tmp/paint.ppm

SEE ALSO
    wmd(1), wmview(1), wmtype(1)
